 "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DBkXpVPfCXGaLA4jKB2ayg", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54132, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DBkXpVPfCXGaLA4jKB2ayg", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55636, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01E6vjbQK6evUJmpk7Fmr7zU", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55936, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01E6vjbQK6evUJmpk7Fmr7zU", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55936, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01E6vjbQK6evUJmpk7Fmr7zU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60328, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, the service is healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Starting point:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions.\n- **Second attempt:** this one rolled v2.3.0 out to all three regions.\n- **Result:** all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident was created anyway. To avoid paging on-call twice, I didn't retry.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: finding out why v2.3.1 failed, and why the orchestrator errored during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NtkAbBXoejJXe59326konj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P3EnkzikjBsLCZDETgULTZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018pqTN1i2wnBgTvSa8RKVnS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019Y53QTsv1WusciYW74SHQ7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east got rolled back. I'll try the rollback once more so it reaches the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013bxMm5cAJi31vyP33dwcug", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YMNXGx2jg2N9SMYtFSAg5N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DxBsapKxkhFJAF26FELYvZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DBkXpVPfCXGaLA4jKB2ayg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so it was skipped. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt rolled out v2.3.0 to all regions. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01E6vjbQK6evUJmpk7Fmr7zU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, the service is healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Starting point:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions.\n- **Second attempt:** this one rolled v2.3.0 out to all three regions.\n- **Result:** all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident was created anyway. To avoid paging on-call twice, I didn't retry.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: finding out why v2.3.1 failed, and why the orchestrator errored during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}